--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 27e5a5b1c5aaf9e4eb4c7c3fd04ba902, type: 3}
  m_Name: Terminal Codes
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  codes:
  - Name: BEER
    Code: 2337
    Mssg: "Ever seen a beer tower before? They\u2019re the best."
  - Name: CHIP
    Code: 2447
    Mssg: "The dipping kind? Those are great with some salsa. Or, wait, did you mean
      the neural kind? Are you sure it\u2019s not all in your head?"
  - Name: FAKE
    Code: 3253
    Mssg: "Maybe. But what\u2019s real?"
  - Name: HELP
    Code: 4357
    Mssg: "Don\u2019t trained divers usually use three letters of morse code for
      this one?"
  - Name: REAL
    Code: 7325
    Mssg: DATA NOT FOUND.
  - Name: SECRET
    Code: 732738
    Mssg: "Secret indeed. Halley\u2019s Bell is rife with them\u2014 I wonder what
      the other keywords are? Here, I\u2019ll give you a hint: 6837. Over."
  - Name: WATCHING
    Code: 92824464
    Mssg: "Watching\u2026 waiting\u2026 commiserating\u2026 you know that one?"
  - Name: E.D.
    Code: 33
    Mssg: He really likes puzzle games, I've heard. If only we were didn't have to
      take the starring role in his.
  - Name: J.O.
    Code: 56
    Mssg: He's always said he's a "goofy goober."
  - Name: L.W.
    Code: 59
    Mssg: Their love for orange makes her easy to pick out in a crowd.
  - Name: ME
    Code: 63
    Mssg: You? A cog in the machine. Just like the rest of us.
  - Name: M.M.
    Code: 66
    Mssg: Every time there's a company dinner, she gets salmon.
  - Name: S.C.
    Code: 72
    Mssg: You know he's close when you hear someone whistling that damn jazz standard.
  - Name: V.1
    Code: 81
    Mssg: "The model of the Bell that you\u2019re in. THC\u2019s original patent."
  - Name: THC
    Code: 842
    Mssg: I don't have anything to say about them. Send in a help request form, why
      don'tcha?
  - Name: YOU
    Code: 968
    Mssg: Me? To you, I'm just an echo of the past.
  - Name: BELL
    Code: 2355
    Mssg: Ding dong!
  - Name: EYES
    Code: 3937
    Mssg: "Feel them on you yet? If not, don\u2019t worry. You will by the end."
  - Name: OVER
    Code: 6837
    Mssg: "Got it all figured out, don\u2019t you? Over."
  - Name: 42069
    Code: 42069
    Mssg: Ha ha. Very funny.
  - Name: KEITH
    Code: 53484
    Mssg: Can't be easy for him, either, but he's a real piece of work. What do you
      think? If you still can.
  - Name: RADIO
    Code: 72346
    Mssg: The only one looking out for you here is you. Pay attention!
  - Name: SORRY
    Code: 76779
    Mssg: Yeah. I think we all are.
  - Name: UNKNOWN
    Code: 8656696
    Mssg: "Into the unknown. That\u2019s definitely the nicest way to phrase this
      experience."
  - Name: NAUTICORE
    Code: 628842673
    Mssg: "You can\u2019t really think that exists. Use your head\u2014 what else
      could NC be? The pieces are all there; you just have to put them together."
  - Name: OPERATOR
    Code: 67372867
    Mssg: "More like \"operated on.\" This isn't on record, but patrons are more
      immersed when the Operator stays quiet, so\u2026 yeah."
  - Name: HALLEYSBELL
    Code: 42553972355
    Mssg: "P:HB was unsuccessful and was discarded. But, looking around, it\u2019s
      cool, right? That\u2019s what I thought, so I tweaked the pitch to get more
      eyes on it and\u2026 now I\u2019m here."
